IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il27-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il27-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito-s40a-divorcee-remarried`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests for s 40A. Row IL-27. Expected values worked by hand from line 1649 before the rules were run; none edited.
-- One point when: a divorcee, he or his spouse paid maintenance to the former spouse, and he is married to another spouse.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — section 40A`

-- The fields: tax year; resident; sex; a divorcee; paid maintenance; married to another spouse; foreign worker.
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `resident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sex`      IS A `A person's sex, for these sections`
      `divorced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paid`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `remarried` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A divorced individual in a tax year, for section 40A`
`in` `the year` `, resident:` `resident` `, sex` `sex` `, divorcee:` `divorced` `, paid maintenance:` `paid` `, married to another:` `remarried` MEANS
    `A divorced individual in a tax year, for section 40A` OF `the year`, `resident`, `sex`, `divorced`, `paid`, `remarried`, FALSE

GIVETH A `A divorced individual in a tax year, for section 40A`
`a foreign worker who meets all the conditions of section 40A` MEANS
    `A divorced individual in a tax year, for section 40A` OF 2026, TRUE, `a man`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE

§§ `The three conditions, for a man`

#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, sex` `a man` `, divorcee:` TRUE `, paid maintenance:` TRUE `, married to another:` TRUE) EQUALS 1
-- Each condition missing on its own: nothing.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, sex` `a man` `, divorcee:` FALSE `, paid maintenance:` TRUE `, married to another:` TRUE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, sex` `a man` `, divorcee:` TRUE `, paid maintenance:` FALSE `, married to another:` TRUE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, sex` `a man` `, divorcee:` TRUE `, paid maintenance:` TRUE `, married to another:` FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- A tax year of the row's range: 2024 answers; 2023 is refused by the general gate.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40A for` (`in` 2024 `, resident:` TRUE `, sex` `a man` `, divorcee:` TRUE `, paid maintenance:` TRUE `, married to another:` TRUE) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 40A for` (`in` 2023 `, resident:` TRUE `, sex` `a man` `, divorcee:` TRUE `, paid maintenance:` TRUE `, married to another:` TRUE) BECAUSE "row IL-27 does not hold the text of these sections for a tax year before 2024"

§§ `Fork F3 — a woman`

-- A woman who meets all three conditions: the default declines.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 40A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, sex` `a woman` `, divorcee:` TRUE `, paid maintenance:` TRUE `, married to another:` TRUE) BECAUSE "section 40A does not say whether a divorcee who is a woman is within it, and here the individual is a woman"
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40A, reading "divorcee" as` `a divorced man only` `and the residence condition as` `no residence condition` `, for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, sex` `a woman` `, divorcee:` TRUE `, paid maintenance:` TRUE `, married to another:` TRUE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40A, reading "divorcee" as` `a divorced person of either sex` `and the residence condition as` `no residence condition` `, for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, sex` `a woman` `, divorcee:` TRUE `, paid maintenance:` TRUE `, married to another:` TRUE) EQUALS 1
-- A woman who fails a condition has nothing on any reading: the default answers.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, sex` `a woman` `, divorcee:` TRUE `, paid maintenance:` FALSE `, married to another:` TRUE) EQUALS 0
-- A man is unaffected by the reading.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40A, reading "divorcee" as` `a divorced man only` `and the residence condition as` `no residence condition` `, for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, sex` `a man` `, divorcee:` TRUE `, paid maintenance:` TRUE `, married to another:` TRUE) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `section 40A — the reading row IL-27 takes of "divorcee"` EQUALS `declined where the individual is a woman`

§§ `Fork F1 — residence; section 48A`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 40A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` FALSE `, sex` `a man` `, divorcee:` TRUE `, paid maintenance:` TRUE `, married to another:` TRUE) BECAUSE "sections 39A, 39B, 40A and 40B name no residence condition, and here residence decides"
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40A, reading "divorcee" as` `declined where the individual is a woman` `and the residence condition as` `no residence condition` `, for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` FALSE `, sex` `a man` `, divorcee:` TRUE `, paid maintenance:` TRUE `, married to another:` TRUE) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40A, reading "divorcee" as` `declined where the individual is a woman` `and the residence condition as` `an Israeli resident only` `, for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` FALSE `, sex` `a man` `, divorcee:` TRUE `, paid maintenance:` TRUE `, married to another:` TRUE) EQUALS 0
-- A non-resident without the point on the facts: nothing on any reading; the default answers.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` FALSE `, sex` `a man` `, divorcee:` FALSE `, paid maintenance:` TRUE `, married to another:` TRUE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 40A for` `a foreign worker who meets all the conditions of section 40A` BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
